In article <CGzJ2t.KEF@iupui.edu>, ssingh@etsun.tech.iupui.edu (Devil's Advocate) writes:

This is mostly in the FAQ.
>1) Tell me where to get the latest version.
  ftp linc.cis.upenn.edu
  login as anonymous
  cd pub/NH3.0
  mget everything
  
>2) Give me detailed instructions on how to install it on a Sun system.
>   this includes the commands for un-tarring stuff.
For the most part, installing on a Sun is easy.  The distribution UNIX
version is for a Sun, so you shouldn't have to change much.  Read the
README file and the sys/unix/Install.unx files carefully.  If you have
trouble, read them again, then maybe post a question.  When I installed
it on a Sun, I had some trouble getting the keypad to work but I figured
it out eventually (that was v3.0j - I've never installed 3.1 on a Sun).

There is a file called unpack.script.  Set the permissions, run this, and 
it should un-tar everything.

>3) Tell me how to set up the score file so everyone can see their score
>   at any time, and not have to start and quit a game.
You can always do this.  Just type 'nethack -s'.

